# --cov-report=json, which the CI coverage job writes to turn the number into a
# step summary. Written into the working directory, so it needs naming here or
# the next `git add` sweeps it into a commit.
coverage.json
Streaming*.json
secrets.json
cookies*.json
# The smoketest's spotapi sessions file (live sp_dc/sp_key cookies) - its docs
# say to keep it beside Database/Spotify/smoketest.py, i.e. inside the tree.
# Only the placeholder shape documentation is allowed through.
session*.json
!Database/Spotify/session.example.json
flask_secret_key.txt

# Runtime data - listening history, images, the database (Spotify session
# cookies included), and the flask secret key file are personal/sensitive and
# must never be committed. Database/Users/ is the pre-1.7.0 name, kept here too
# since existing local checkouts won't have renamed it until their next start.
secrets/
Database/Data/
Database/Users/
autoImport/
tmp/
TestData/
